"0da544d1-339b-52fe-93ad-b7cc9037f9ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466349} {:answer/id #uuid "52870258-d972-5635-9243-e534e273e365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "52870258-d972-5635-9243-e534e273e365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466350} :answer-field/id #uuid "00f9d316-8393-5444-ad7d-3bfe9ded25fc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467018}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e65967cd-c336-53ba-a105-1c4f34ff015c" :question/math-academy-id "q-335824" :question/problem "![](images/96/96df34b3f844ee5abace182769011a3b4b2e413100fbca4cf25e829ca67948cc.png)\n\nConsider the phase line shown above. Which of the following differential equations could have this phase line?\n\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(y-2)^{2}(y-4)$\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(y-2)(y-4)(y-6)$\n- $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=(y-2)^{2}(y-4)(y-6)$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that all three differential equations are of the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y).\n$$\n\nThe phase line gives us the following information:\n\n- The equilibrium solutions are $y=2,$ $y=4$ and $y=6.$\n\n- $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,2)\\cup (2,4)\\cup (6,\\infty ).$\n\n- $f(y)$ is negative for $y\\in (4,6).$\n\nWith this in mind, let's study each of the given equations.\n\n- We start by considering\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(y-2)^{2}(y-4).\n$$\n\nIn this case, $f(y)=(y-2)^{2}(y-4),$ and the equilibrium solutions are $y=2,4$ only.\n\nTherefore, equation I does not have the given phase line.\n\n- Next, we consider\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=(y-2)(y-4)(y-6).\n$$\n\nIn this case, $f(y)=(y-2)(y-4)(y-6),$ and the equilibrium solutions are $y=2,4,6.$\n\nHowever, we note that $f(y)<0$ for $y\\in (-\\infty ,2).$ This does not correspond to the arrows shown on the phase line.\n\nTherefore, equation II does not have the given phase line.\n\n- Finally, we consider ${y}^{′}=(y-2)^{2}(y-4)(y-6).$\n\nFirst, we see that $f(y)=(y-2)^{2}(y-4)(y-6),$ so $f(y)=0$ if $y=2,4,6.$ So, the equilibrium solutions correspond to those shown in the phase line.\n\nNow, we can construct a sign table for $f(y)$ as follows:\n\n|  | $(-\\infty ,2)$ | $(2,4)$ | $(4,6)$ | $(6,\\infty )$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $(y-2)^{2}$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $y-4$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| $y-6$ | $-$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| $f(y)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\nSo, we have that $f(y)$ is negative for $y\\in (4,6),$ and $f(y)$ is positive for $y\\in (-\\infty ,2)\\cup (2,4)\\cup (6,\\infty ).$\nTherefore, equation III has the given phase line.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229149 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e69075-ef65-5a18-b911-601b515a9a84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying d'Alembert Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050185 :topic/id #uuid "34c91ba2-4c7e-5fc4-8f4a-760354b8b507" :topic/math-academy-id 6692 :topic/title "d'Alembert Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3957a9c2-7880-520a-ade2-12150916fb87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466351} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc83860-f67b-5819-93de-844ddfa746d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cc83860-f67b-5819-93de-844ddfa746d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466352} :answer-field/id #uuid "cdd77ac5-51c1-5cc5-80e6-bf64f824a81c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467019} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7971b98-4412-5cc0-966e-124b4ff95cf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466353} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3b873e-9d8e-5426-95b8-9bb145cec8bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e7971b98-4412-5cc0-966e-124b4ff95cf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466353} :answer-field/id #uuid "6206ecd4-d346-5c00-a75c-f1bfc159bcf0" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467020} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a592ea9b-4320-545f-a7dc-64fa58ef1c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466355} {:answer/id #uuid "9282e269-a2f9-55a6-b6e5-cdfdeef3f9bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9282e269-a2f9-55a6-b6e5-cdfdeef3f9bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466356} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5bf6c60-1d15-5fd3-aa6e-0b7ca8f8930f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467021}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "870fa3ac-a172-57d1-b18b-7584f7771a44" :question/math-academy-id "q-337223" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a d'Alembert differential equation?\n- **I.** $y=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{′})+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+({y}^{′})^{2})$\n- **II.** $y{y}^{′}={x}^{3}y+1$\n- **III.** $y-x({y}^{′})^{2}+{e}^{{y}^{′}}=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nNote that, in the special case where $f({y}^{′})={y}^{′},$ the equation reduces to a Clairaut differential equation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with \n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{′}),\\,g({y}^{′})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+({y}^{′})^{2}).\n$$\n\n- Equation II is *not* a d'Alembert differential equation. Solving for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{{y}^{′}-{x}^{3}},\n$$\n\nwhich cannot be written in the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\n- Equation III is a d'Alembert differential equation. Isolating the variable $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=x({y}^{′})^{2}-{e}^{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwhich is of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229149 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e69075-ef65-5a18-b911-601b515a9a84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying d'Alembert Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050185 :topic/id #uuid "34c91ba2-4c7e-5fc4-8f4a-760354b8b507" :topic/math-academy-id 6692 :topic/title "d'Alembert Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a02ccdc-2375-5a29-92c3-175669696a30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466357} {:answer/id #uuid "11662cff-37ca-5ba0-b40e-e2c0d725bb55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11662cff-37ca-5ba0-b40e-e2c0d725bb55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466358} :answer-field/id #uuid "126fc659-7e57-551e-bc93-ef28c513d685" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467022} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97f40bf1-591e-5d73-85f3-b29a5f32ce92" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466359} {:answer/id #uuid "f8bd5955-f774-52bd-b780-94d4bf4a0faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8bd5955-f774-52bd-b780-94d4bf4a0faa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466360} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfc81d91-111a-514d-b961-21566c875273" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467023} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e8b90f8-06d8-5a16-a730-dd085e5c9a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466361} {:answer/id #uuid "118c087b-f708-57cf-8c14-20affbaf50c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e8b90f8-06d8-5a16-a730-dd085e5c9a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466361} :answer-field/id #uuid "8caaf6a5-5787-5790-8251-e027231c41a2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467024}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76e64e6f-7a8a-5b8b-bac6-612af4c245fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-337226" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a d'Alembert differential equation?\n- **I.** $y=x({y}^{′})^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′})$\n- **II.** $y+x({y}^{′})^{2}={2}^{{y}^{′}}$\n- **III.** $y{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+x$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nNote that, in the special case where $f({y}^{′})={y}^{′},$ the equation reduces to a Clairaut differential equation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with\n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=({y}^{′})^{2},\\,g({y}^{′})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′}).\n$$\n\n- Equation II is a d'Alembert differential equation. Isolating the variable $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=-x({y}^{′})^{2}+{2}^{{y}^{′}},\n$$\n\nwhich is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with \n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=-({y}^{′})^{2},\\,g({y}^{′})={2}^{{y}^{′}}.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is *not* a d'Alembert differential equation. Solving for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{{y}^{′}-{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhich cannot be written in the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229149 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e69075-ef65-5a18-b911-601b515a9a84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying d'Alembert Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050185 :topic/id #uuid "34c91ba2-4c7e-5fc4-8f4a-760354b8b507" :topic/math-academy-id 6692 :topic/title "d'Alembert Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36b237d8-7d4d-5e24-befe-7a80c5d38d2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466363} {:answer/id #uuid "735cb599-e2c8-5ee7-b807-b331f751b08a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36b237d8-7d4d-5e24-befe-7a80c5d38d2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466363} :answer-field/id #uuid "be9da2e5-2b72-5b17-8d1b-04d3b32f6046" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0ae4c64-97d0-59e7-923e-63a8cc3bb56e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466365} {:answer/id #uuid "3f18c69f-a7ee-53b5-8d23-5752580cb512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466366}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f18c69f-a7ee-53b5-8d23-5752580cb512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466366} :answer-field/id #uuid "908ed06d-7486-5f3c-8e01-70700dbd5867" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467026} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c1647fe-12c1-5bff-9ce6-6af8f1e927e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466367} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef692b8-fc85-5879-8425-ed2a283f36c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ef692b8-fc85-5879-8425-ed2a283f36c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466368} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6669f95-5c93-5291-8fb0-49131a8d0fd1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1b52c57b-852c-58e2-ae93-cc78b2af7920" :question/math-academy-id "q-337229" :question/problem "Which of the following equations is a d'Alembert differential equation?\n- **I.** $y{y}^{′}={x}^{2}y+x$\n- **II.** $y+x({y}^{′})^{2}={e}^{{y}^{′}}$\n- **III.** $y=x({y}^{′})^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′})$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A differential equation is a d'Alembert differential equation if it can be expressed in the form\n\n$$\ny=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}),\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are differentiable functions of ${y}^{′}.$ \n\nNote that, in the special case where $f({y}^{′})={y}^{′},$ the equation reduces to a Clairaut differential equation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Equation I is *not* a d'Alembert differential equation. Solving for $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{x}{{y}^{′}-{x}^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhich cannot be written in the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′}).$\n\n- Equation II is a d'Alembert differential equation. Isolating the variable $y,$ we get\n\n$$\ny={e}^{{y}^{′}}-x({y}^{′})^{2},\n$$\n\nwhich is of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with\n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=-({y}^{′})^{2},\\,g({y}^{′})={e}^{{y}^{′}}.\n$$\n\n- Equation III is a d'Alembert differential equation of the form $y=xf({y}^{′})+g({y}^{′})$ with\n\n$$\nf({y}^{′})=({y}^{′})^{2},\\,g({y}^{′})=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{y}^{′}).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229149 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "c2e69075-ef65-5a18-b911-601b515a9a84" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying d'Alembert Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050185 :topic/id #uuid "34c91ba2-4c7e-5fc4-8f4a-760354b8b507" :topic/math-academy-id 6692 :topic/title "d'Alembert Differential Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60388ce7-8ec6-5a7f-b1f6-56340f1366d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466369} {:answer/id #uuid "f793d3af-a158-5d86-a2e2-6d0442d7e8ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466370}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60388ce7-8ec6-5a7f-b1f6-56340f1366d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466369} :answer-field/id #uuid "32de82c9-72f1-5d35-93ea-792ea1bfa150" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467028} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9cbb407b-f5d9-5917-a922-0d1fb0bba992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466371} {:answer/id #uuid "0eed2a02-9245-5adf-894d-d23bc862d952" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218