dent :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f4fa353d-a0fb-5d32-a867-d6df2715a793" :question/math-academy-id "q-337765" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n- **I.** ${D}_{1}(y)=(x-1)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy$\n- **II.** ${D}_{2}(y)=y\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- **III.** ${D}_{3}(y)=4\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}-{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)=x-1$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=2x.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the first term is $y,$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a third-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}(x)=4,{f}_{2}(x)=0,{f}_{1}(x)=-{x}^{2},$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311882 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050537 :topic/id #uuid "51e12769-3848-5c84-bd86-1c35f7ad69b3" :topic/math-academy-id 6707 :topic/title "Linear Differential Operators"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b6efbb1-6753-589e-8c8f-6ca7cb7e3bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466387} {:answer/id #uuid "040366b7-a201-5d51-9814-b5b3c5650657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "040366b7-a201-5d51-9814-b5b3c5650657" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466388} :answer-field/id #uuid "1df85e67-865c-5823-a44e-24957be174fc" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467037} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a5f650cf-fe4e-5312-9a1c-c6ce2309470c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466389} {:answer/id #uuid "24eede71-8855-5bc8-88c8-a011df7187ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466390}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5f650cf-fe4e-5312-9a1c-c6ce2309470c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466389} :answer-field/id #uuid "591cf1f2-ae7f-5252-a115-04dc8a4e10af" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467038} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5d9b6ef4-9a0c-5948-8bd8-17d41816039d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466391} {:answer/id #uuid "cc201f03-759e-58f5-a5b5-9dc2404a7466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cc201f03-759e-58f5-a5b5-9dc2404a7466" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466392} :answer-field/id #uuid "f12e1391-d624-5025-baed-903820006794" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8ea3d35e-7e2f-5e81-99fa-fd738c89805d" :question/math-academy-id "q-337773" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n- **I.** ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\sqrt{x}y$\n- **II.** ${D}_{2}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- **III.** ${D}_{3}(y)={e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,y$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}},{f}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=\\sqrt{x}.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the last term is $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy),$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)={e}^{x},$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311883 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050537 :topic/id #uuid "51e12769-3848-5c84-bd86-1c35f7ad69b3" :topic/math-academy-id 6707 :topic/title "Linear Differential Operators"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5741d0ef-f988-591f-a348-2e58e9d2111c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466393} {:answer/id #uuid "bec72ab2-96ad-509b-acd9-a831f59510b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5741d0ef-f988-591f-a348-2e58e9d2111c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466393} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a87cfe5-7519-5962-8097-2e8019998439" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467040} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "522e0fbb-288a-5ce0-ae54-cac4e30d1b73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466395} {:answer/id #uuid "9b297c94-292d-513d-a8ed-db1f13a0b690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b297c94-292d-513d-a8ed-db1f13a0b690" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466396} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7823a75-1b1d-5e30-99bd-538b43fa4598" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467041} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4e5044d-466d-568e-ab18-0274b043fbe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466397} {:answer/id #uuid "84a851d3-78ac-5a58-a6e9-b1f29f54a6c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4e5044d-466d-568e-ab18-0274b043fbe7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466397} :answer-field/id #uuid "00dd682e-53d3-56b8-8067-598af7d82ba2" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467042}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a7fcf4e-fdda-501c-b765-bd8e87f5aae0" :question/math-academy-id "q-337774" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n- **I.** ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- **II.** ${D}_{2}(y)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{e}^{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}y$\n- **III.** ${D}_{3}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y)\\,y$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the second term is $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y),$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x),{f}_{1}(x)={e}^{x},$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the second term is $x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(y),$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050537 :topic/id #uuid "51e12769-3848-5c84-bd86-1c35f7ad69b3" :topic/math-academy-id 6707 :topic/title "Linear Differential Operators"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c2809fc-3f64-562a-a005-f78c451d2a2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466399} {:answer/id #uuid "8d7c266e-1c56-54b2-aaf6-367d55a3327f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c2809fc-3f64-562a-a005-f78c451d2a2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466399} :answer-field/id #uuid "0058b6d7-5961-597c-afb4-bdac6ce6ffa1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467043} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5488c63e-26ae-5ad8-aab9-74b5d8d20c80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466401} {:answer/id #uuid "d207ba86-61cb-5bc7-8449-9f29de274726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d207ba86-61cb-5bc7-8449-9f29de274726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466402} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2c69489-9ae9-5e41-a79b-4b3353ee2f14" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "70d4b961-effc-5654-b426-2322d8a2bd14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466403} {:answer/id #uuid "5fb604ea-6a7f-54d2-887c-5edae00dba6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70d4b961-effc-5654-b426-2322d8a2bd14" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466403} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa5fd7ab-beb9-5ce4-8b2d-e61c300f6b86" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467045}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "47d8bb1c-4d46-5c7b-bec5-01c857be1d48" :question/math-academy-id "q-337777" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n- **I.** ${D}_{1}(y)=xy\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$\n- **II.** ${D}_{2}(y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{x}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{e}^{x}y$\n- **III.** ${D}_{3}(y)=\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y)\\,y$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the first term is $xy,$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),{f}_{1}(x)={x}^{2},$ and ${f}_{0}(x)={e}^{x}.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is *not* linear. The coefficient of the last term is $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(y),$ which depends on $y$ and therefore fails linearity.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311885 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229138 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5976004-053f-58ec-9d75-54d43a419397" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linear Differential Operators Using the General Form" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050537 :topic/id #uuid "51e12769-3848-5c84-bd86-1c35f7ad69b3" :topic/math-academy-id 6707 :topic/title "Linear Differential Operators"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8462488e-272b-5772-bf64-9aa1638edb21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466405} {:answer/id #uuid "06728173-b51c-55c4-92d8-9851289d57bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "06728173-b51c-55c4-92d8-9851289d57bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466406} :answer-field/id #uuid "caa1bd4a-3eba-56e1-a3ba-6e63da10f9e6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467046} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bc57e6f5-5ce9-51db-a506-35f8fe3453e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466407} {:answer/id #uuid "634f6c08-51bc-5474-b7ad-cca79735d829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "634f6c08-51bc-5474-b7ad-cca79735d829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466408} :answer-field/id #uuid "e33b4fc0-086e-5fab-be31-3e3d8f7b2025" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467047} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e38e3054-6ed9-56c7-8585-41217d71f832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466409} {:answer/id #uuid "1168cf38-73e5-5de7-a26b-6306956051c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1168cf38-73e5-5de7-a26b-6306956051c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466410} :answer-field/id #uuid "10a51316-22f5-5b3e-9744-bdf00aa12c02" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a6ed137-ea67-591f-bf1a-a0d1b0037ea7" :question/math-academy-id "q-337778" :question/problem "Which of the following are linear differential operators?\n\nI. ${D}_{1}(y)=\\frac{1}{x+1}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,y$\n\nII. ${D}_{2}(y)=\\sqrt{x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-2y$\n\nIII. ${D}_{3}(y)=2\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{e}^{x}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,y$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "An $n$th-order differential operator $L$ is linear if it is of the following form:\n\n$$\nL(y)={f}_{n}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n}}+{f}_{n-1}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{n-1}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{n-1}}+⋯+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwhere each ${f}_{i}$ is a function of $x$ only. \n\nWith that in mind, let's check each operator.\n\n- Operator ${D}_{1}$ is linear. It is a first-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}(y)={f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{1}(x)=\\frac{1}{x+1}$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{2}$ is linear. It is a second-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}(y)={f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{2}(x)=\\sqrt{x},{f}_{1}(x)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x),$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=-2.$\n\n- Operator ${D}_{3}$ is linear. It is a third-order linear differential operator of the form\n\n$$\n{D}_{3}(y)={f}_{3}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{3}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{3}}+{f}_{2}(x)\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}}+{f}_{1}(x)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{f}_{0}(x)y\n$$\n\nwith ${f}_{3}(x)=2,{f}_{2}(x)={e}^{x},{f}_{1}(x)=0,$ and ${f}_{0}(x)=-\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050537 :topic/id #uuid "51e12769-3848-5c84-bd86-1c35f7ad69b3" :topic/math-academy-id 6707 :topic/title "Linear Differential Operators"} :activity/title "Linear Differential Operators" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433323} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186433345}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152273 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a926134-0870-5528-985d-2c92e71158f4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Second-Order Linear ODEs" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050677 :topic/id #uuid "5e132315-9606-5b30-bee3-61f0209d40c4" :topic/math-academy-id 2548 :topic/title "Introduction to Second-Order Linear ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c09d354a-972a-5465-a370-382725d7b170" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466411} {:answer/id #uuid "931baba1-25ba-5aa4-838d-d4d1a6ee68e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} 