?\n- **I.** $x{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+4y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2x,\\,y(-1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=0$\n- **II.** ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+y=8$\n- **III.** $x{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-3y={e}^{x},\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=4$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem.  It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-1$ and $x=2$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$)."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129314 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66d19e98-522f-5db2-b340-0f35ba2ece23" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Linear System of Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048451 :topic/id #uuid "a0acd569-aa75-5c03-9c8e-bc8f5d31d263" :topic/math-academy-id 2086 :topic/title "Introduction to Systems of Linear ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a70dcada-b35b-5ea2-81ae-9a14d25bb8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466459} {:answer/id #uuid "88da30f1-bf22-5037-8e6b-e01c1e416d0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466460}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a70dcada-b35b-5ea2-81ae-9a14d25bb8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466459} :answer-field/id #uuid "d48ff154-ddc8-5f49-895a-ba6e05cc17d9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1f76d3-3f1b-57ee-a715-2a68791121ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466461} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b9cf44-ea2d-5de0-ab90-3dd1ef729c2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d1f76d3-3f1b-57ee-a715-2a68791121ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466461} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad382fdb-f756-5f62-acee-f78ba500a79b" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467074} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1a1fd3e-868f-5e84-81d9-7cb26b5f7a05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466463} {:answer/id #uuid "ac97a1fe-d8c8-51aa-ba4d-06599a39af00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ac97a1fe-d8c8-51aa-ba4d-06599a39af00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466464} :answer-field/id #uuid "719b9600-1552-5231-8306-c5f2edac961e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467075}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27876a51-c9f8-5f4d-9c9b-be85b540294f" :question/math-academy-id "q-339539" :question/problem "Which of the following are first-order linear systems of ODEs?\n- **I.** $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}(t){x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=-{x}_{1}(t)+3{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n- **II.** $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=5{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}^{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=6{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n- **III.** $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}{x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)+1 \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=\\sqrt{7}\\,{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t)+3t\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is not a first-order linear system of ODEs since it contains the term ${x}_{1}(t){x}_{2}(t).$\n\n- System II is not a first-order linear system of ODEs since it contains the term ${x}_{2}^{2}(t).$\n\n- System III is a first-order linear system of ODEs since it can be written in the standard form, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}, &  & b(t)=-2, &  & f(t)=1, \\\\ c(t)=\\sqrt{7}, &  & d(t)=5, &  & g(t)=3t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314792 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129314 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66d19e98-522f-5db2-b340-0f35ba2ece23" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Linear System of Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048451 :topic/id #uuid "a0acd569-aa75-5c03-9c8e-bc8f5d31d263" :topic/math-academy-id 2086 :topic/title "Introduction to Systems of Linear ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c93f72ea-a72b-534b-8b07-68dd630ed592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466465} {:answer/id #uuid "eb4276fe-b5e7-5574-9671-cc628285f741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466466}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb4276fe-b5e7-5574-9671-cc628285f741" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466466} :answer-field/id #uuid "83fd42ce-5dfd-5e09-a6ac-41488ad2578f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467076} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24108b29-e70d-58fb-a033-49aaedd4e644" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466467} {:answer/id #uuid "490664f0-bbaa-576a-be50-ee9ee5989469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "490664f0-bbaa-576a-be50-ee9ee5989469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466468} :answer-field/id #uuid "5e318dbe-bf05-5a37-b0f2-d45b795f3fec" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9faa87d0-2c58-5b56-b62c-9beeaa0bb339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466469} {:answer/id #uuid "a7f1d784-e5f4-5c2f-a451-9e8b401c4e28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9faa87d0-2c58-5b56-b62c-9beeaa0bb339" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466469} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b3c8a51-7071-55bf-9a02-177f4c98b266" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467078}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "686f5a84-c1ca-551b-b5e9-fd8d6a7feafb" :question/math-academy-id "q-339540" :question/problem "Which of the following are first-order linear systems of ODEs?\n- **I.** $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t)\\,{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{1}(t)+\\sqrt{3}\\,t\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n- **II.** $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=cos\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}){x}_{1}(t)+{13}^{2}{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=9{x}_{1}(t)-\\pi {x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n- **III.** $\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=2{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &={x}_{1}^{2}(t)+{x}_{2}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear system of differential equations with two dependent variables is a system of equations that takes the following standard form:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) &=a(t){x}_{1}(t)+b(t){x}_{2}(t)+f(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) &=c(t){x}_{1}(t)+d(t){x}_{2}(t)+g(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $a(t),$ $b(t),$ $c(t),$ $d(t),$ $f(t),$ and $g(t)$ are known functions, and\n\n- ${x}_{1}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)$ are unknown functions (dependent variables).\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is a first-order linear system of ODEs since it can be written in the standard form, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t), &  & b(t)=1, &  & f(t)=0, \\\\ c(t)=2, &  & d(t)=0, &  & g(t)=\\sqrt{3}\\,t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System II is a first-order linear system of ODEs since it can be written in the standard form, where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t)=cos\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{8}), &  & b(t)={13}^{2}, &  & f(t)=0, \\\\ c(t)=9, &  & d(t)=-\\pi , &  & g(t)=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- System III is not a first-order linear system of ODEs since it contains the terms ${x}_{1}^{2}(t)$ and ${x}_{2}^{2}(t).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129314 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "66d19e98-522f-5db2-b340-0f35ba2ece23" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Linear System of Differential Equations" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048451 :topic/id #uuid "a0acd569-aa75-5c03-9c8e-bc8f5d31d263" :topic/math-academy-id 2086 :topic/title "Introduction to Systems of Linear ODEs"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8934ab18-fc42-5a90-aa01-d1800e4a26b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466471} {:answer/id #uuid "08740ab6-9867-5e2e-b769-36866bdbac2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "08740ab6-9867-5e2e-b769-36866bdbac2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186466472} :answer-field/id #uuid "42093f82-f83c-5e65-9c21-4eec23c1c817" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467079} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uui