y dividing by $(x+3)(x-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+3)(x-2){y}^{″}+(x-1){y}^{′}+y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{x-1}{(x+3)(x-2)}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{(x+3)(x-2)}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{x-1}{(x+3)(x-2)}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+3)(x-2)}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check the analyticity of these functions at the given points.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=-3,$ since both denominators at $x=-3$ equal zero. So, $x=-3$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Both* functions are analytic about $x=0.$ So, $x=0$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Both* functions are analytic about $x=1.$ So, $x=1$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317233 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124676 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "12a9f9cf-06f6-51b8-ba41-a8b6300a5c2b" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Ordinary and Singular Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049703 :topic/id #uuid "0cc17781-65fe-5316-8a26-4416142da248" :topic/math-academy-id 1880 :topic/title "Regular Singular Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4282fcd2-2c7f-5161-a429-d0d3cc73b3a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467184} {:answer/id #uuid "7c11ecc9-2e47-55eb-bc7c-6991f8740ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467185}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c11ecc9-2e47-55eb-bc7c-6991f8740ed6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467185} :answer-field/id #uuid "95c76cce-4f16-5a11-953d-a84b0bf34558" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468313} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "025a4359-7a91-5137-8a09-70dc4cc50fc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467186} {:answer/id #uuid "af99a91b-8b55-5cb3-b703-b1019b4894f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "025a4359-7a91-5137-8a09-70dc4cc50fc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467186} :answer-field/id #uuid "561f39f8-8c80-5e37-8858-4860215fee54" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468314} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bc3c5b1-62c2-5279-b911-f456156feb98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467188} {:answer/id #uuid "7100ed54-fb7e-5377-af86-dd97886b7438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bc3c5b1-62c2-5279-b911-f456156feb98" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467188} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ec5aa21-a5de-5c6a-8b93-17eafe2d2a28" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3c8079ad-949a-5a26-9868-d6f6b2551b3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-342296" :question/problem "$$\n(x+2)(x-1){y}^{″}+(x-3){y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is an **ordinary** point of the differential equation above?\n- **I.** $x=0$\n- **II.** $x=-2$\n- **III.** $x=1$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The point $x=a$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nif both coefficients $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, $x=a$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $(x+2)(x-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)(x-1){y}^{″}+(x-3){y}^{′}+y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{x-3}{(x+2)(x-1)}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{(x+2)(x-1)}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{x-3}{(x+2)(x-1)}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{(x+2)(x-1)}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check the analyticity of these functions at the given points.\n\n- *Both* functions are analytic about $x=0.$ So, $x=0$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=-2,$ since both denominators at $x=-2$ equal zero. So, $x=-2$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\n- *Neither* function is analytic about $x=1,$ since both denominators at $x=1$ equal zero. So, $x=1$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317234 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e7d1368-06ee-5135-b9f4-d3d4d2756b32" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regular and Irregular Singular Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049703 :topic/id #uuid "0cc17781-65fe-5316-8a26-4416142da248" :topic/math-academy-id 1880 :topic/title "Regular Singular Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e9a4c96-43fa-5287-87ab-e21349de37d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467190} {:answer/id #uuid "276c2b5f-dd00-52b7-8c1d-6ce75f463861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "276c2b5f-dd00-52b7-8c1d-6ce75f463861" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467191} :answer-field/id #uuid "fe7daa95-4d2d-517d-9d71-1edb7ff485f9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468316} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af517c28-aae7-53be-b6d7-3b41927254b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467192} {:answer/id #uuid "92f7e79b-d815-5ee2-9318-38d9f2b65ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92f7e79b-d815-5ee2-9318-38d9f2b65ab5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467193} :answer-field/id #uuid "8226dddc-7d72-59c3-b2bb-d0c8e17007a2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468317} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171850f3-b5d7-5b49-9740-52d5f9f4f4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467194} {:answer/id #uuid "222fcf3d-3109-5f47-a245-e67afddc63cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "171850f3-b5d7-5b49-9740-52d5f9f4f4d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467194} :answer-field/id #uuid "072ca5e1-ee75-57ee-8c43-02549fc0ad4f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fac58339-a2d8-5129-8e48-737c1bfcbe88" :question/math-academy-id "q-342299" :question/problem "$$\n({x}^{2}-1){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The functions $P(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-1}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{2}-1}$ are analytic about $x=0.$\n- **II.** The functions $xP(x)$ and ${x}^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=0.$\n- **III.** The point $x=0$ is a **regular** singular point of the differential equation.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A singular point $x=a$ of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nis regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $({x}^{2}-1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}-1){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+{e}^{x}y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-1}{y}^{′}+\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{2}-1}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}-1}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{{x}^{2}-1}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check each statement in turn.\n\n- Both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=0.$ So, statement I is true.\n\n- Since $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=0,$ multiplying them by $x$ and ${x}^{2},$ respectively, they remain analytic about $x=0.$ Therefore, statement II is true.\n\n- Since statement I is true, $x=0$ is an ordinary point, not a singular point. Thus, statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317235 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e7d1368-06ee-5135-b9f4-d3d4d2756b32" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regular and Irregular Singular Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049703 :topic/id #uuid "0cc17781-65fe-5316-8a26-4416142da248" :topic/math-academy-id 1880 :topic/title "Regular Singular Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b7793ce5-15ff-5b47-a37d-9da5824b876c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467196} {:answer/id #uuid "b3f71b86-58a1-549c-8d6f-3b8b5e3a54dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b7793ce5-15ff-5b47-a37d-9da5824b876c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467196} :answer-field/id #uuid "8409e5b2-c7a3-5cdb-888a-155f06ea7493" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468319} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6299e52e-8932-5c1a-a081-893c3d68d775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467198} {:answer/id #uuid "fd4fb28e-9720-5ef3-a59c-b822e0d712e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd4fb28e-9720-5ef3-a59c-b822e0d712e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467199} :answer-field/id #uuid "6238fb21-5d0c-51a9-a39c-230145dd17ce" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468320} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95e1469b-461d-569b-b247-6fdc19f5ee8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467200} {:answer/id #uuid "ead7cfc0-2c13-575b-a9ba-0f6e4e25e709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95e1469b-461d-569b-b247-6fdc19f5ee8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467200} :answer-field/id #uuid "457626e7-0327-5d43-9dd1-76fd6a6f102e" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "182bf2f2-0927-5526-ba0f-19a051c0f88c" :question/math-academy-id "q-342300" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The functions $P(x)=\\frac{1}{x}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}$ are analytic about $x=0.$\n- **II.** The functions $xP(x)$ and ${x}^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=0.$\n- **III.** The point $x=0$ is an **irregular** singular point of the differential equation.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A singular point $x=a$ of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nis regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by ${x}^{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check each statement in turn.\n\n- Since the denominators of both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ vanish at $x=0,$ they are *not* analytic about $x=0.$ So, statement I is false.\n\n- The function\n\n$$\nxP(x)=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}=1\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=0,$ and the function\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}Q(x)={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nis also analytic about $x=0.$ Therefore, statement II is true.\n\n- Since statement I is false, $x=0$ is a singular point. Also, since statement II is true, it follows that $x=0$ is a **regular** singular point. Thus, statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317236 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e7d1368-06ee-5135-b9f4-d3d4d2756b32" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regular and Irregular Singular Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049703 :topic/id #uuid "0cc17781-65fe-5316-8a26-4416142da248" :topic/math-academy-id 1880 :topic/title "Regular Singular Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ff0f11c-1635-5de0-bb9b-318cebabf753" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467202} {:answer/id #uuid "6520152a-550e-51db-86ef-17b9ab825abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6520152a-550e-51db-86ef-17b9ab825abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467203} :answer-field/id #uuid "13fa2c6b-783a-5c29-aac3-7169a61b11d3" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468322} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd795e8f-2f45-5bf9-b4bc-933c0ff71777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467204} {:answer/id #uuid "896bb7e4-bb10-564c-aaf2-508a2088e0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "896bb7e4-bb10-564c-aaf2-508a2088e0a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467205} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f4ae311-b3ea-59e5-8d8e-80008abdc27d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468323} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3106d23-a3a7-56f4-bec3-143517651ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467206} {:answer/id #uuid "2a9a6b7f-1c09-5e68-91a2-6a7cb268ab7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3106d23-a3a7-56f4-bec3-143517651ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467206} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9a64153-0821-5729-8176-a4052e15c45b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468324}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d598b560-2b94-5f0a-b115-9618b72a3e44" :question/math-academy-id "q-342303" :question/problem "$$\n({x}^{2}+1){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The functions $P(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}$ are analytic about $x=-1.$\n- **II.** The functions $(x+1)P(x)$ and $(x+1)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-1.$\n- **III.** The point $x=-1$ is a **regular** singular point of the differential equation.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "A singular point $x=a$ of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nis regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $({x}^{2}+1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({x}^{2}+1){y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nLet's now check each statement in turn.\n\n- Both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-1.$ So, statement I is true.\n\n- Since $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=-1,$ multiplying them by $(x+1)$ and $(x+1)^{2},$ respectively, they remain analytic about $x=-1.$ Therefore, statement II is true.\n\n- Since statement I is true, $x=-1$ is an ordinary point, not a singular point. Thus, statement III is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186317237 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124677 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9e7d1368-06ee-5135-b9f4-d3d4d2756b32" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Regular and Irregular Singular Points" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049703 :topic/id #uuid "0cc17781-65fe-5316-8a26-4416142da248" :topic/math-academy-id 1880 :topic/title "Regular Singular Points"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b04bcb67-6e20-5fca-ae58-78333e4bfd8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450542} {:answer/id #uuid "ea01357a-c8e8-5b4b-a9eb-1d9411d901a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref