A,$ $B,$ $R,$ and $ϕ$ are constants.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Because the motion is undamped and the system experiences resonance, the forcing frequency equals the natural frequency $\\omega .$\n\nThe external force is $f(t)=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t),$ which is sinusoidal with frequency $3.$ Therefore,\n$\\omega =3.$\n\nThe complementary solution for the associated simple harmonic motion equation can be written in three different forms:\n\n1\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n2\\. ${y}_{c}=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\omega t+ϕ)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)$\n\n3\\. ${y}_{c}=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nAt resonance, a sinusoidal trial at frequency $\\omega $ duplicates the complementary solution, so we multiply by $t$ and take a resonant particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)).\n$$\n\nBy substituting the particular solution and $\\omega =3$ into the differential equation, ${y}^{″}+{\\omega }^{2}y=f(t),$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[(6D-9Ct)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-(6C+9Dt)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)]+9t(C\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+D\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)) & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t) \\\\ 6D\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)-6C\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t) & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, $C=0$ and $D=\\frac{5}{3}.$ \n\nSo, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}(t)=\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).\n$$\n\nFinally, then, the general solution is given by the sum of the complementary and particular solutions. So, it can be written in any of the following forms:\n\n1\\. $y=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n2\\. $y=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t+ϕ)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\n3\\. $y=A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3t)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)+\\frac{5}{3}t\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$\n\nSolutions I, II, and III match the forms above.\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048966 :topic/id #uuid "cfd9de67-b6d3-5aac-81ab-498c732e22a6" :topic/math-academy-id 6720 :topic/title "Resonance in Vibrating Systems"} :activity/title "Resonance in Vibrating Systems" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517486} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518302}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319150 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050426 :topic/id #uuid "47f4b767-dd8b-5a07-a614-8ff85185d0eb" :topic/math-academy-id 1861 :topic/title "Linear Dependence and Independence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dfbe41c-73e7-5f56-8ce0-fab54ad50616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467286} {:answer/id #uuid "f341d81e-bf26-5210-b2f0-54763ec31dc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f341d81e-bf26-5210-b2f0-54763ec31dc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467287} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf382855-5600-5598-8164-5bd2d028dbce" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468364} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5748a03b-cb2b-5a33-8622-5e3f40a35b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467288} {:answer/id #uuid "114a823e-72e5-59c8-8d1c-742efeb3c793" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5748a03b-cb2b-5a33-8622-5e3f40a35b20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467288} :answer-field/id #uuid "a8ad6860-dfb4-5757-801b-d9850857f91a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468365} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "861d0168-10b8-592b-ae21-e0ad86936c5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467290} {:answer/id #uuid "8b18b4b9-7ea2-5329-bec7-e618d7c6db3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b18b4b9-7ea2-5329-bec7-e618d7c6db3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467291} :answer-field/id #uuid "e64595f5-23c8-52a5-9fe4-2c3e7d56935c" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468366}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c6e61ad-5f9a-5a1b-a420-c0ce7a3cc35c" :question/math-academy-id "q-34700" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions.\n- **II.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n- **III.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 6 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the matrix above, we conclude that the basic variables are ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, while ${x}_{3}$ is the free variable. \n\nSince there is one free variable, the equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has an infinite number of nonzero solutions, which means that the vectors are linearly dependent. \n\nTherefore, statement II is false, while statements I and III are true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050426 :topic/id #uuid "47f4b767-dd8b-5a07-a614-8ff85185d0eb" :topic/math-academy-id 1861 :topic/title "Linear Dependence and Independence"} :activity/title "Linear Dependence and Independence" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572303} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572785}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319157 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119925 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52a45814-d1e2-5948-b7bd-69dcaf6cd0eb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Linearly Independent and Dependent Sets Using Row Reduction" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050426 :topic/id #uuid "47f4b767-dd8b-5a07-a614-8ff85185d0eb" :topic/math-academy-id 1861 :topic/title "Linear Dependence and Independence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae02702d-cbaa-5d1a-aa13-b56e62ddc9bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467292} {:answer/id #uuid "8beff570-6962-575d-83e8-fba6dd1988f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8beff570-6962-575d-83e8-fba6dd1988f9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467293} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa0b3013-1ffe-5f8b-9931-4aa005775eb9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468367} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bf5efc0-d0b0-5ab3-9ccc-0f8c702a8c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467294} {:answer/id #uuid "16afad4c-9e4f-5af8-9660-d5618a99eb7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bf5efc0-d0b0-5ab3-9ccc-0f8c702a8c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467294} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f0fc8a3-12a0-5de6-975a-2b93da0b8887" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468368} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c50196f4-ea00-5775-b667-c59254cbbc4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467296} {:answer/id #uuid "b5af3771-12a3-55ad-b5c8-8f960c1dfa83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5af3771-12a3-55ad-b5c8-8f960c1dfa83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467297} :answer-field/id #uuid "496267ed-e481-5779-8831-27ec9128e7bf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b1abddd4-93e9-501d-bf47-b8161bdb88cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-34714" :question/problem "Consider the following vectors:\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{2}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,{a}_{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n \n\nAssume that ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}$ are real numbers. Which of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** The equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ has only the trivial solution ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$\n- **II.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly dependent.\n- **III.** The vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},$ and ${a}_{3}$ are linearly independent.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "We say that three vectors ${v}_{1},{v}_{2},$ and ${v}_{3}$ are *linearly independent* if the only solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{v}_{1}+{x}_{2}{v}_{2}+{x}_{3}{v}_{3}=0\n$$\n\nis ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0.$ Otherwise, the vectors are *linearly dependent*.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\nThe equation ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=0$ corresponds to the system \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system, we create its augmented matrix and reduce it using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=0.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}+(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=0\n$$\n\nand, substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSince ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0$, we get that the set ${{a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}}$ is linearly independent.\n\nTherefore, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050426 :topic/id #uuid "47f4b767-dd8b-5a07-a614-8ff85185d0eb" :topic/math-academy-id 1861 :topic/title "Linear Dependence and Independence"} :activity/title "Linear Dependence and Independence" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572303} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572762}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319199 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124490 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca956d3e-37a8-5f0f-a062-97d0567d54e6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Bases of Abstract Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048552 :topic/id #uuid "a92f5097-81a3-51a2-90e4-397763d967f0" :topic/math-academy-id 1909 :topic/title "Bases in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26f0f70b-01ad-54d8-8ebf-898c5fe4a5ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467298} {:answer/id #uuid "fb802504-b985-574f-8a9d-3bec9d243fe1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467299}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26f0f70b-01ad-54d8-8ebf-898c5fe4a5ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467298} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e9feac7-9064-55a0-bfec-cd6e08f02bc2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468370} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "899ffc4b-f3bc-5a5a-b2b2-a4baa23129c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467300} {:answer/id #uuid "49992a1c-d3d1-51dc-acc4-0664a7fe647f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "899ffc4b-f3bc-5a5a-b2b2-a4baa23129c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467300} :answer-field/id #uuid "e01f4bda-c99b-5a8d-abab-2d7127981cca" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468371} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "288f07a5-4416-53ed-8a09-84f609c31a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467302} {:answer/id #uuid "3e5dced2-a28c-53a7-be07-84415c967344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467303}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "288f07a5-4416-53ed-8a09-84f609c31a09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467302} :answer-field/id #uuid "353db63d-6718-5fd5-b88a-f76be029806b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4fa1c1b6-aa0b-5eb1-b0a4-3972a58dc98e" :question/math-academy-id "q-34768" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}$ and ${R}^{2}$, respectively. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$\n- **II.** ${{b}_{3},{b}_{1},{b}_{1}+{b}_{3}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$\n- **III.** ${x,{b}_{2},{c}_{1}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ and $C$ are bases, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ and $C$ are maximally linearly independent sets in ${R}^{2}$ and ${R}^{3},$ respectively, and\n\n- $B$ spans ${R}^{3},$ while $C$ spans ${R}^{2}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$, any vector of ${R}^{2},$ including the given vector $x,$ can be written as a linear combination of ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$ This means that ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2},x}$ is linearly dependent and therefore, cannot be a basis.\n\n- Statement II is false. The set ${{b}_{3},{b}_{1},{b}_{1}+{b}_{3}}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the third vector is a linear combination of ${b}_{3}$ and ${b}_{1}.$ This means that the set is linearly dependent and therefore, cannot be a basis.\n\n- Statement III is false. The set ${x,{b}_{2},{c}_{1}}$ is not a basis of ${R}^{3}$ because the set contains vectors from another vector space.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124509 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050996 :topic/id #uuid "7821b684-8118-5d42-9459-ebb20010e0ff" :topic/math-academy-id 1868 :topic/title "The Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d0064e2-7095-50a4-9f68-f09ccda97572" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450548} {:answer/id #uuid "87590c0b-b8a7-56c3-9915-4df9e724e9df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87590c0b-b8a7-56c3-9915-4df9e724e9df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450549} :answer-field/id #uuid "71819ef2-7ff5-5f57-beb5-0822cdadf30b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451228} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a417e97-6614-5b7a-935f-3f703efe4728" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450550} {:answer/id #uuid "705d803b-01fe-5cbc-9e39-520b711450ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "705d803b-01fe-5cbc-9e39-520b711450ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450551} :answer-field/id #uuid "dd4d11a6-d574-56be-a1ff-bf51d5086a53" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451229} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b9dcaeb-747d-5dcd-9605-08aa07e4d4fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450552} {:answer/id #uuid "7e2164d5-f2d9-5323-8150-cf625cddb533" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b9dcaeb-747d-5dcd-9605-08aa07e4d4fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450552} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d6cdc8f-65c5-5192-ac5b-16ea774e5f9b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6b1d1e88-f02a-5243-9bdc-9d244b4db578" :question/math-academy-id "q-34902" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.$\n- **II.** If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.$\n- **III.** If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=3.$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $1$ pivot column and $1$ non-pivot column. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. The matrix $B$ has $1$ pivot column and $2$ non-pivot columns (namely, the $2$nd and $3$rd columns). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The matrix $C$ has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050996 :topic/id #uuid "7821b684-8118-5d42-9459-ebb20010e0ff" :topic/math-academy-id 1868 :topic/title "The Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix"} :activity/title "The Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186490500} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491223}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186319352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124509 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f020b27f-1cd4-550b-a83a-2afbb7e5db72" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Dimension of the Null Space of Matrices Using Inspection" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050996 :topic/id #uuid "7821b684-8118-5d42-9459-ebb20010e0ff" :topic/math-academy-id 1868 :topic/title "The Dimension of the Null Space of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e278eb04-9ea2-5844-b05e-b7780ac79ae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450554} {:answer/id #uuid "9c39f12c-2213-5317-b25b-2b94303ac001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c39f12c-2213-5317-b25b-2b94303ac001" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450555} :answer-field/id #uuid "2574fec4-c774-5e83-88c2-54c6e3934238" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451231} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e20627b5-0399-56be-bf11-b108f477de32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450556} {:answer/id #uuid "fd76fc07-6256-5abb-ada4-e6122e1a413e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e20627b5-0399-56be-bf11-b108f477de32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450556} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4b81185-37e8-5204-a76c-9cca612b39b1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451232} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b008e94-bd7d-587f-b70b-14f6d36a4468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450558} {:answer/id #uuid "f5a6b4d9-1c23-50e1-93df-86fd6c5da0a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b008e94-bd7d-587f-b70b-14f6d36a4468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450558} :answer-field/id #uuid "9da1ea97-6d5c-56ad-aad8-3bac4d1c60b6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451233}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "56ebc46d-299b-5fda-a402-a93bacc04806" :question/math-academy-id "q-34973" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** If $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.$\n\n- **II.** If $B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(B))=3.$\n\n- **III.** If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ then $\\text{dim(Null}(C))=2.$" :question/worked-solution "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The matrix $A$ has $3$ pivot columns and $2$ non-pivot columns. So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(A))=2.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. The matrix $B$ has $3$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $4$th column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(B))=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The matrix $C$ has $2$ pivot columns and $1$ non-pivot column (namely, the $2$nd column). So, \n\n$$\n\\text{dim(Null}(C))=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/title "Quiz 11" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045460 :db/ident :activity.type/assessment} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547297} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186548182}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321014 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124490 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ca956d3e-37a8-5f0f-a062-97d0567d54e6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements About Bases of Abstract Vector Spaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048552 :topic/id #uuid "a92f5097-81a3-51a2-90e4-397763d967f0" :topic/math-academy-id 1909 :topic/title "Bases in Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49e71ad1-ea91-5baf-ac78-a0a822a0304d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467304} {:answer/id #uuid "23617b73-b0c1-56a3-94d8-5e95a1ec53e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467305}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23617b73-b0c1-56a3-94d8-5e95a1ec53e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467305} :answer-field/id #uuid "f98b53cd-b6ce-5f24-81a4-7fdcfa0d6dcf" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468373} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fa1b6d3-f46b-546a-b479-70f15e2991a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467306} {:answer/id #uuid "5b607205-ca72-5983-b64d-742e571d204a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5b607205-ca72-5983-b64d-742e571d204a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467307} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bca7760-9dab-5b33-a4da-148b71b29bed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468374} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c3aa2298-16cc-5a08-bf62-ff6520fa43f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467308} {:answer/id #uuid "da723a23-ee4b-5c25-9bd8-061a2e359b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c3aa2298-16cc-5a08-bf62-ff6520fa43f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467308} :answer-field/id #uuid "5a6e4e94-b485-52c8-b42a-9cc118288739" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468375}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d3cfa016-2023-56d8-80a8-ced31694c0b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-35263" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ and $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ be bases of ${R}^{3}$ and ${R}^{2}$, respectively. \n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n- **I.** ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{2}+{b}_{3}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$\n- **II.** ${3{c}_{2},{c}_{1}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{2}$\n- **III.** ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},x}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Since $B$ and $C$ are bases, the following properties must hold:\n\n- $B$ and $C$ are maximally linearly independent sets in ${R}^{2}$ and ${R}^{3},$ respectively, and\n\n- $B$ spans ${R}^{2},$ while $C$ spans ${R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}({b}_{2}+{b}_{3}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{3}){b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, since ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ is linearly independent, gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{2}+{b}_{3}}$ spans $V$ since any linear combination of vectors from $B$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{2}+{b}_{3}}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{b}_{1}+{x}_{2}{b}_{2}+{x}_{3}{b}_{3}={x}_{1}{b}_{1}+({x}_{2}-{x}_{3}){b}_{2}+{x}_{3}({b}_{2}+{b}_{3})\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, the equation\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(3{c}_{2})+{x}_{2}{c}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nis equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3{x}_{1}){c}_{2}+{x}_{2}{c}_{1} & =0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich, since ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$ is linearly independent, gives\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⟹\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{2} &=0.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nAlso, ${3{c}_{2},{c}_{1}}$ spans $V$ since any linear combination of $C$ can be expressed as a linear combination of ${3{c}_{2},{c}_{1}}:$\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2}={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+\\frac{{x}_{2}}{3}(3{c}_{2})\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ is a basis of ${R}^{3}$, any vector of ${R}^{3},$ including the given vector $x,$ can be written as a linear combination of ${b}_{1},$ ${b}_{2}$ and ${b}_{3}.$ This means that ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3},x}$ is linearly dependent and therefore, cannot be a basis.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186321043 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d847ec9-c379-5013-ab77-a9b92dc8ca27" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Matrix With a Given Rank by Inspection" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050028 :topic/id #uuid "26e7d665-1fe7-5eaf-8ec8-486cb95ff36f" :topic/math-academy-id 1867 :topic/title "The Rank of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c38e2b1e-6c94-5624-8794-4c613a255924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467310} {:answer/id #uuid "5d54ebf0-003a-5f1c-bd7e-8c9967853943" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c38e2b1e-6c94-5624-8794-4c613a255924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467310} :answer-field/id #uuid "e26dd5b4-e353-584a-b82f-a7001a7ceafd" :answer-field/key "A" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468376} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80281206-d511-56fb-abc8-2ec2bd14982e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467312} {:answer/id #uuid "0ee50a33-bcd1-57ca-af8a-fea5667b18e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80281206-d511-56fb-abc8-2ec2bd14982e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467312} :answer-field/id #uuid "2eb96f6f-4c8d-5ec7-a8ea-8d4572cc6d20" :answer-field/key "B" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468377} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9723544-78fc-5712-9c8f-ca9dda43b954" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467314} {:answer/id #uuid "c1730f02-53e8-5c11-881b-06d6506cf09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1730f02-53e8-5c11-881b-06d6506cf09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467315} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a295ee6-c8e9-5be1-8d44-50156c244fcb" :answer-field/key "C" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468378}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "43599508-ddd2-50d6-b640-692e29bcfb0e" :question/math-academy-id "q-35283" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $6?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 & 5 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that a matrix of rank $6$ must have at least $6$ columns and at least $6$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $A$ since it has only $5$ columns and the matrix $B$ since it has only $4$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $6$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $6$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050028 :topic/id #uuid "26e7d665-1fe7-5eaf-8ec8-486cb95ff36f" :topic/math-academy-id 1867 :topic/title "The Rank of a Matrix"} :activity/title "The Rank of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186454901} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186455524}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323674 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124511 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "084a0a83-5ce6-5184-beb7-8ae7b4f1a799" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Using the Invertible Matrix Theorem" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049340 :topic/id #uuid "ecf075bf-6d18-5a77-93a9-57ef73f45115" :topic/math-academy-id 1869 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of Dimension, Rank and Nullity"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ccb0567-0495-5c74-8699-bab086a64809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450560} {:answer/id #uuid "62954330-fa79-5088-bd4b-cb797b88fe25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ccb0567-0495-5c74-8699-bab086a64809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450560} :answer-field/id #uuid "c34e741f-afd5-539e-89ed-87f3b75f5ff9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46523043-bc55-5cb6-b33f-a37a5b648d6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450562} {:answer/id #uuid "2d38beb7-b0db-523b-99bb-2bb27ec73198" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46523043-bc55-5cb6-b33f-a37a5b648d6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450562} :answer-field/id #uuid "d46ab9df-f1e2-5ca8-bca4-a8a7559c9764" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451235} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd58a89b-6f9b-54a1-881b-e354c7de0b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450564} {:answer/id #uuid "2d103fe3-6dbf-53c9-a8ce-da05a06b3a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d103fe3-6dbf-53c9-a8ce-da05a06b3a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450565} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f8121ca-3a46-557f-84a4-3de651e3583d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9288acd6-ddf2-55d8-ba92-e1c27cfdfe7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-35425" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true, given that $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix and $v=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}$  is a solution of the equation $Ax=0?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\text{dim(Null}(A))=0$\n- **II.** $A$ is invertible\n- **III.** $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5$" :question/worked-solution "Since $A$ is a $5\\times 5$ matrix, the invertible matrix theorem states the following:\n\n$$\nA\\text{ is }\\text{invertible}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{Col}(A) &=\\mathbb{R}^{5} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Col}(A)) &=5=\\operatorname{rank}(A) \\\\ \\operatorname{Null}(A) &=\\{0\\} \\\\ \\dim(\\operatorname{Null}(A)) &=0=\\operatorname{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement in turn. \n\n- Statement I is false. Since $v\\ne 0$ and $Av=0,$ \nthen $v\\in \\text{Null}(A)$ and, therefore, $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $\\text{dim(Null}(A))\\ne 0,$ then according to the invertible matrix theorem, the matrix $A$ can't be invertible.\n\n- Statement III is true. Since $A$ is not invertible, then by the invertible matrix theorem, we must have $\\text{rank}(A)\\ne 5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323702 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192781 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1094661c-8c7c-5f85-b731-4dadb0aec310" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Using Set Notation Are Subspaces" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048337 :topic/id #uuid "96874e3b-8b97-5c33-995d-d34a9d3daf21" :topic/math-academy-id 4077 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e0cec0f5-50a0-5db7-aa24-c8f6e6f46576" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467316} {:answer/id #uuid "84637b0b-e6d4-5bf8-8d2a-0889fc35f79a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84637b0b-e6d4-5bf8-8d2a-0889fc35f79a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467317} :answer-field/id #uuid "3580a9f0-52f8-5185-8668-b0142e7a463c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468379} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4781a47-7159-598f-bde4-83c8c11de3e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467318} {:answer/id #uuid "7de9877f-5787-5cf1-9cf3-6d2942ba95b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4781a47-7159-598f-bde4-83c8c11de3e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467318} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5f1fc60-d17d-5814-b04d-4e79e98e1504" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468380} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "470f0416-0b89-5555-aeca-66f06e23ece5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467320} {:answer/id #uuid "3e03d669-cae3-5262-bdca-b0bd34428d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e03d669-cae3-5262-bdca-b0bd34428d27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467321} :answer-field/id #uuid "15500526-9977-5c61-a2b5-2c48a155e044" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468381}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3d143826-9093-5bc1-bb87-8034a4c54f58" :question/math-academy-id "q-35599" :question/problem "Which of the following sets is a subspace of ${R}^{2}?$\n- **I.** $A={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 0}$\n- **II.** $B={⟨x,y⟩\\in {R}^{2}:x=\\frac{1}{2}y+2}$\n- **III.** $C={0}$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each of the subsets.\n\n- The set $A$ is a subspace. There is only one vector in ${R}^{2}$ that satisfies the equation ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 0,$ namely, the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩.$ So, $A={0}$, which is a special subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- The set $B$ is not a subspace because it does not contain the zero vector. Indeed, $0=⟨0,0⟩$ does not satisfy the equation $x=\\frac{1}{2}y+2$ since $0\\ne \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0+2.$\n\n- The set $C$ is a subspace. This subset has only one element, the zero vector $0=⟨0,0⟩,$ which is a special subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323703 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3fe3596-340e-5155-bed3-cf25f5843d70" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether Sets Represented Graphically Are Subspaces in Two-Dimensional Space" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048337 :topic/id #uuid "96874e3b-8b97-5c33-995d-d34a9d3daf21" :topic/math-academy-id 4077 :topic/title "Subspaces of N-Dimensional Space: Geometric Interpretation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0970f7c9-0267-5fd4-9880-d41ae3a79463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467322} {:answer/id #uuid "4f237964-f389-5bd6-8aac-aa282034aac0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0970f7c9-0267-5fd4-9880-d41ae3a79463" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467322} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5afcb2c-0b40-564c-94ff-ab2c6514204c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468382} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e4fd8e4-2e3e-5610-9911-e8b5d526828a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467324} {:answer/id #uuid "c173b593-8813-5ead-a8f2-2b0d20818dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c173b593-8813-5ead-a8f2-2b0d20818dc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467325} :answer-field/id #uuid "a377b320-87d3-55f5-bdfe-2d4bec9a251e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468383} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40effee0-f377-5750-80bf-ca89c9343a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467326} {:answer/id #uuid "c9dc1941-779c-5fcc-9d45-969d4645ba9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40effee0-f377-5750-80bf-ca89c9343a9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467326} :answer-field/id #uuid "aca2e0c7-307a-569b-a613-32617eec1ceb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2aec92e-c3f4-5cb5-bae0-799d4d7e0d99" :question/math-academy-id "q-35600" :question/problem "![](images/ec/ec79ffa15b3ed25d8f439f575e1cdffc3122ae1d82e1b55500a6e5e2e17cf4fc.png)\n\nWhich of the diagrams shown above represent subspaces of ${R}^{2}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\nIf none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each diagram in turn.\n\n- Diagram I does not represent a subspace.  Every subspace must contain the origin,  but from the diagram, we can easily see that the origin is not in the subset.\n\n- Diagram II represents a subspace. It represents the whole plane, which is considered a special subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\n- Diagram III represents the whole plane ${R}^{2}$  without the origin. But every subspace must contain the origin, so Diagram III is not a subspace of ${R}^{2}.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124628 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cb02b67c-90d9-5baf-b00e-590e9271d89e" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Closed Under Addition and Scalar Multiplication" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b16ecbe9-c123-5857-9769-f9dac3faf9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467328} {:answer/id #uuid "f26b27de-130c-507d-93c7-a96ecd84d877" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b16ecbe9-c123-5857-9769-f9dac3faf9b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467328} :answer-field/id #uuid "71d59c2d-9307-5d0c-ae75-e6fa043a32b8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "105b805f-626c-510e-9607-294f6d3052af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467330} {:answer/id #uuid "c645ff3c-1f3e-52e7-a675-1735a28d5139" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "105b805f-626c-510e-9607-294f6d3052af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467330} :answer-field/id #uuid "15c9c1d7-7c6f-570e-bd49-f923b5d980c6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468386} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48a80cf6-9c47-5285-b19c-99279bdd2a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467332} {:answer/id #uuid "cf7cf8b3-7bac-53b6-8c28-aef339f0ac97" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "48a80cf6-9c47-5285-b19c-99279bdd2a43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467332} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed7fca77-deb6-591f-ae0c-b458de0a03bc" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468387}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18aef812-0fac-5da2-8d8b-c2702b3daa12" :question/math-academy-id "q-35663" :question/problem "Let $S$ be the set of all polynomials with real coefficients and whose degree is greater than or equal to $2.$  Which of the following statements are true? \n- **I.** $f(x)\\in S,$ where $f(x)=2x.$\n- **II.** For every $p(x),q(x)\\in S,$ we have $p(x)+q(x)\\in S.$\n- **III.** The set is closed under addition.\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "Let's verify the statements one at a time.\n\n- Statement I is false. The set $S$ contains only polynomials whose degree is greater than or equal to $2.$ However, \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{deg}⁡(2x)=1\\ne 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=2x\\notin S.$\n\n- Statement II is false. There exist functions in $S$ such that their sum is *not* in $S.$ For example, let $p(x)=x+{x}^{2}$ and $q(x)=x-{x}^{2}.$ Notice that both these functions belong to $S$ since $\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p(x))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡(q(x))=2\\ge 2.$ However,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{deg}⁡(p(x)+q(x))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡((x+{x}^{2})+(x-{x}^{2}))=\\operatorname{deg}⁡(2x)=1≱2.\n$$\n\nHence, $p(x)+q(x)\\notin S.$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since statement II is false, the set is *not* closed under addition.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements are true.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323715 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124480 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b1a557d6-52f3-5df3-8088-5b875296e72e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049723 :topic/id #uuid "0e15397e-6c32-508c-b6ea-90f1a9e5a237" :topic/math-academy-id 1904 :topic/title "Identifying the Pivot Columns of a Matrix"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e64682-e33b-5167-b977-f5b3b286bbd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574405} {:answer/id #uuid "dda07581-f82c-574b-bf17-ca5951e59677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186574406 :task-item/_responses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186574142 :task-item/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323715} :task-item/status {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045571}}]}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dda07581-f82c-574b-bf17-ca5951e59677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 