:answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1299406e-f829-5fd4-8425-b85b65f7d4fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438186} :answer-field/id #uuid "926e0c3c-cd97-51cc-9746-082bf755755f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439122} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af648e1c-82fc-509a-86a4-bb4d1e1ddc6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438188} {:answer/id #uuid "820b9e7c-c94e-5f14-8992-67543fc3d809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438189}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "820b9e7c-c94e-5f14-8992-67543fc3d809" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438189} :answer-field/id #uuid "b77279af-afdb-5c4b-87f9-0e122b9f690b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439123}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "69ab5c8f-74d2-578a-ab14-a3f834908b70" :question/math-academy-id "q-36002" :question/problem "![](images/c5/c51c5a4de562e5a3301ea76afc6af57b459acd4c46e5c65d54afc226d883a137.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-3,0]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (-3,1)$\n- **III.** $x\\in [0,3)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,0]$ and $x\\in [0,3).$ Indeed, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/00/00a80dde24ca012e0282362224c8b63764f5e149a8bfcda9c76ff4eb958fa93a.png)\n\n \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $x\\in (-3,1)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/9e/9ea54918e2ef4310b58e9cf8a0c9b1f9757a404d97dbbfd9e5b037af2193f38c.png)\n\n \n\nHence, the correct answer is 'I and III only''."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323737 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049731 :topic/id #uuid "0f127f4a-3cf5-5736-90b8-9817b73eb050" :topic/math-academy-id 1889 :topic/title "Invertible Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e496da34-dbaf-5186-8e70-09599d4e42f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438190} {:answer/id #uuid "681351b2-3b37-513b-bb0f-7040b33c72b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "681351b2-3b37-513b-bb0f-7040b33c72b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438191} :answer-field/id #uuid "482ac440-f320-503b-99d7-eb74230b2bc9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439124} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04eefd7c-a896-59e8-91d0-cbdf4380aedc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438192} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcd2979-e497-5817-b474-8325f90706bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04eefd7c-a896-59e8-91d0-cbdf4380aedc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438192} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d241933-0dfc-5f49-ba97-b39545dc4a25" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439125} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88c808cf-3477-5af3-b1f2-145c26c92a7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438194} {:answer/id #uuid "8503b8fd-888a-50aa-943d-954d7bdf8c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8503b8fd-888a-50aa-943d-954d7bdf8c66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438195} :answer-field/id #uuid "4056b817-e800-5678-8e9e-22469e604236" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439126}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "544516cf-cdec-5de8-af07-1ff7e5be101e" :question/math-academy-id "q-36004" :question/problem "![](images/15/1597ad53471d0d9b44812c5caa31bcb160cfa150d1df9a9314447fa49e62ccff.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in [-6,0]$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in [-6,4)$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [4,10)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in [-6,0]$ and $x\\in [4,10).$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/7c/7cb282e3fa66af801ff03816973d5f5f1d0cb41e39d08a8addd27d7aa9c5b9df.png)\n\n      \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $[-6,4]$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/00/000953609a7b3e13ad09473ead62f96aa895c7f94aa618884e69883595004fd4.png)\n\n \n\n Therefore, the correct answer is \"I  and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049731 :topic/id #uuid "0f127f4a-3cf5-5736-90b8-9817b73eb050" :topic/math-academy-id 1889 :topic/title "Invertible Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6dd990f-2330-5d0c-81b4-6370f4d92329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438196} {:answer/id #uuid "d3d6745b-46d2-5323-8629-40d7481f8ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3d6745b-46d2-5323-8629-40d7481f8ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438197} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fa5f1a4-0dd6-545a-95f5-013d457374c6" :answer-field/key "I" :