estion.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aef31e6b-2918-5842-b5c4-348781827064" :question/math-academy-id "q-36010" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=|x-2|+1,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$\n- **II.** $x\\in (1,\\infty )$\n- **III.** $x\\in (2,4]$" :question/worked-solution "The graph of the function $f(x)=|x-2|+1$ can be obtained in the following way:\n\n- Take the curve $y=|x|.$\n\n- Translate it by $2$ units to the right,  to get $y=|x-2|.$\n\n- Finally, translate $y=|x-2|$ by $1$ unit up to get $f(x)=|x-2|+1.$\n\n![](images/ce/ceab1637313ae53869cc1e59f6a56ad6cb920a83dffba482558b696188df0d36.png)\n\nA function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-\\infty ,1]$ and $x\\in (2,4].$ On these intervals, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/a4/a47169838785b6f4ac78253252bcedc3c2cb752a655feac9945e20dd40563b4f.png)\n\n  \n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not invertible on the interval $x\\in (1,\\infty ).$ On this interval, some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/14/14ed35294e1179ffd9efaf87fa8ac1eb99853a7da344e462c2cb0dda74c3b78f.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049731 :topic/id #uuid "0f127f4a-3cf5-5736-90b8-9817b73eb050" :topic/math-academy-id 1889 :topic/title "Invertible Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88cfd433-113f-5181-b46c-34920cbe5bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438208} {:answer/id #uuid "92c8406c-f814-57d1-83d4-a13a818e5eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92c8406c-f814-57d1-83d4-a13a818e5eb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438209} :answer-field/id #uuid "0273b980-43eb-564c-872d-0589397d574e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439133} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890e79b7-dfdd-538c-8e9a-7abc3f553b47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438210} {:answer/id #uuid "2981f923-7ad3-5ee6-93aa-64b271aaa970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438211}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2981f923-7ad3-5ee6-93aa-64b271aaa970" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438211} :answer-field/id #uuid "5568fe44-2db6-5364-963c-2b0dbd971f58" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439134} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c1bcc67-9524-5941-9eb2-6c123826210d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438212} {:answer/id #uuid "cfff16d0-eaff-5775-853f-d6b2f96cf631" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438213}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c1bcc67-9524-5941-9eb2-6c123826210d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438212} :answer-field/id #uuid "25f018c0-f200-5146-8568-3810e8f2e7b5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439135}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d31db013-e3f7-5fe2-aefa-8428da418673" :question/math-academy-id "q-36011" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b02c2e94e144935f0ff96846cd51b5a969fa8f884a7ca1d09abb231b7c945232.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-4,-2)$\n\n- **II.** $x\\in [-2,3]$\n\n- **III.** $x\\in [-3,3]$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test.  \n\n- The given function is invertible on each of the intervals $x\\in (-4,-2)$ and $x\\in [-2,3].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/53/53fe88780b2ccb7522d2f1baa711162ec99300c2a2d4da29bba9ca532026cd07.png)\n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on  the interval $x\\in [-3,3]$  because some lines will  intersect the curve at more than one point.\n\n![](images/63/63cee4fc05ab17a8e69d9bfae578fa83c24d73e4677065a54a33a25e0871e718.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323748 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124472 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3bd13aa5-83a8-5b23-96cb-ea665039ea30" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying an Invertible Function From Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 