uid "b28f36fb-3166-55fa-8439-85a4e2c30bf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438225}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9b43604-8edf-57f2-b9de-096dcbcc5dd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438224} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c22e257-18b9-5973-9c9f-ae85ffec73b4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8aef7162-d0e5-5631-91ce-694e2ecc3ef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438226} {:answer/id #uuid "c1588c7f-143f-535f-b50f-e63a5091e059" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8aef7162-d0e5-5631-91ce-694e2ecc3ef2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438226} :answer-field/id #uuid "56db77a8-773c-594c-afa2-0b04cacc3d8a" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439142}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0429905-029f-5585-ac21-8d23fa4141fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-36063" :question/problem "![](images/1d/1dd593e8b48b13ec512a3e0c823ec0aaac4f5341bd519c7bb9b04648f95f4251.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above correspond to an invertible function?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible if and only if it's a one-to-one function. To determine which of the functions are one-to-one, we use the horizontal line test.\n\n![](images/2a/2a68cbeceea9173ab7a53d334d073e9779b048ad8946fd3ff81b09adb79cee98.png)\n\nFrom the above, we see that:\n\n- For graph II, a horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line. Therefore, graph II shows a one-to-one function. As a result, this function is invertible.\n\n- For graphs I, III and IV, some horizontal lines intersect the curve more than once. These are not one-to-one functions. As a result, they are not invertible."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323749 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124473 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ffd143c8-a993-5d0b-85a5-821d6482ae60" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given Its Graph" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049731 :topic/id #uuid "0f127f4a-3cf5-5736-90b8-9817b73eb050" :topic/math-academy-id 1889 :topic/title "Invertible Functions"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "efc69b98-00eb-5840-b90d-c96ba4931e4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438228} {:answer/id #uuid "4ccd2d26-a281-5b97-9b06-263136be07dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4ccd2d26-a281-5b97-9b06-263136be07dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438229} :answer-field/id #uuid "559a6aac-97fe-50a0-8beb-d1323671d7f8" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439143} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40a97abe-d55d-5007-b4fd-6937cc34e17a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438230} {:answer/id #uuid "b173d1e1-4b30-5d88-8de6-73fd6e00131b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b173d1e1-4b30-5d88-8de6-73fd6e00131b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438231} :answer-field/id #uuid "6639d61d-bf93-5072-838b-4370ba49c0ed" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fcc16d7-b530-54ef-9b90-9c7275e5931d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438232} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf0f901-76be-5f84-b0ee-c5cd9c1a5306" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438233}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fcc16d7-b530-54ef-9b90-9c7275e5931d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438232} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f0537b4-3665-5585-a12b-bb1d508ad121" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6815ae09-6f05-5b7b-9ca9-f709c3e26769" :question/math-academy-id "q-36066" :question/problem "![](images/e2/e2065775ae6372e8c820b5e2f19f6f105e032dcd37db1e32e04af5bfa6a4faf9.png)\n\nOn which of the following intervals is the function $f(x)$ (shown above) invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x\\in (-3,-2]\\cup (2,4)$\n- **II.** $x\\in (0,2]$\n- **III.** $x\\in [1,4)$" :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it's a one-to-one function on that interval. To determine the intervals on which the function is invertible, we use the horizontal line test. \n\n- The given function is invertible on the intervals $x\\in (-3,-2]\\cup (2,4)$ and $x\\in (0,2].$ Indeed, any horizontal line will intersect the curve at most once, no matter where we draw the line.\n\n![](images/3c/3c5bc724ee29aee7bef2790012bf0e73ce1ed087134213dbad36a670fd136a36.png)\n\n        \n\n- The given function is **not** invertible on the interval $[1,4)$  because some horizontal lines will intersect the curve more than once.\n\n![](images/03/03b9d70513a4ef99b39c9f05d0c0ac803f8e5611d0967015e9c1d9c0f45bd418.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I  and II only\"." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049731 :topic/id #uuid "0f127f4a-3cf5-5736-90b8-9817b73eb050" :topic/math-academy-id 1889 :topic/title "Invertible Functions"} :activity/title "Invertible Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560353} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186561098}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323750 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115235 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9923c6c3-e425-54ae-a533-09421d5578cb" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a True Statement Given a 2x2 Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050906 :topic/id #uuid "70425962-eba3-5483-950c-6e00e8bba0c0" :topic/math-academy-id 1730 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of 2x2 Systems of Equations"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f00f19b1-a5d9-5f3f-892f-2e3d8e66d32c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450566} {:answer/id #uuid "f24b70da-3d6e-5768-987e-5a6a1111b77e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f00f19b1-a5d9-5f3f-892f-2e3d8e66d32c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450566} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac17f050-593c-55c0-be4c-979e6666933f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451237} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40c3344c-65d7-58be-ae26-42bb9b9f586a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450568} {:answer/id #uuid "740835e0-32e5-50d4-b9e7-dfc4013e2ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450569}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "740835e0-32e5-50d4-b9e7-dfc4013e2ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450569} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0e7cf2e-0dcc-5b45-a214-fc4802e94260" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451238} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f9e3557-049b-5e3a-bce9-8906dde445a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450570} {:answer/id #uuid "9efcb6d2-5f9b-556f-ba0b-a54c998fb8e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1f9e3557-049b-5e3a-bce9-8906dde445a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450570} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fd7516a-09ae-5918-99f5-dc75f2fb3320" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b252a44d-8417-5bdc-8a9b-ad6e81276b7c" :question/math-academy-id "q-36075" :question/problem "Let \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $det(A)=0$\n- **II.** $Ax=0$ has the unique  solution $⟨0,0⟩$\n- **III.** $⟨5,-4⟩$ is a solution to $Ax=0$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =3\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-6\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement II is true by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false. Again,  according to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050906 :topic/id #uuid "70425962-eba3-5483-950c-6e00e8bba0c0" :topic/math-academy-id 1730 :topic/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of 2x2 Systems of Equations"} :activity/title "The Invertible Matrix Theorem in Terms of 2x2 Systems of Equations" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494315} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495176}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323771 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054816 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d132801-b9cc-5c0c-a8fa-0c8b840c05bd" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Sets Containing a Given Element" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049887 :topic/id #uuid "1bbcbfec-d0a8-5419-81c9-b34aaaaaa84f" :topic/math-academy-id 47 :topic/title "Special Sets"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b95a8c9-ef0a-5052-a30e-f82b7c845cdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467334} {:answer/id #uuid "3273b5a4-d168-5995-b944-97e01461a450" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467335}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b95a8c9-ef0a-5052-a30e-f82b7c845cdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467334} :answer-field/id #uuid "66f6fb2a-591a-5d66-9453-5da4821d956f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468388} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8be760ab-0a6d-5fd5-b5f7-486e24062b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467336} {:answer/id #uuid "dc1f8050-3523-515b-aa66-37c702a2cfce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8be760ab-0a6d-5fd5-b5f7-486e24062b50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467336} :answer-field/id #uuid "58eae98c-17a5-501e-b42a-508d606b40f6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468389} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2daafc7-c6b4-54a7-ab4c-97cbc22bcecb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467338} {:answer/id #uuid "9c78a2ba-3305-5a3e-b9ad-5c2cb9f0b0e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2daafc7-c6b4-54a7-ab4c-97cbc22bcecb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467338} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3f61f9e-c2cd-5c5e-b608-37e69bc49a60" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468390} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e083057-d217-55e7-bc22-fb619e13da4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467340} {:answer/id #uuid "fb356de8-7756-5c98-9f14-b75bff8799b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e083057-d217-55e7-bc22-fb619e13da4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467340} :answer-field/id #uuid "576ee637-38c3-5fb3-a0d3-dbe771a24c36" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f51862bd-578b-533f-86e5-e297bb989e9a" :question/math-academy-id "q-36244" :question/problem "To which of the following sets do all the real numbers belong?\n- **I.** ${Z}^{-}$\n- **II.** $N$\n- **III.** $Q$\n- **IV.** ${Q}^{-}$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- The set ${Z}^{-}$ contains all the negative integer numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to ${Z}^{-},$ so ${Z}^{-}$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set $N$ contains all the natural numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to $N,$ so $N$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set $Q$ contains all the rational numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to $Q,$ so $Q$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\n- The set ${Q}^{-}$ contains all the negative rational numbers. However, real numbers as, for instance, $\\sqrt{2}$ don't belong to ${Q}^{-},$ so ${Q}^{-}$ does *not* contain the real numbers. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\""}]
